### Phase 2 — Complete the validated protocol and explicit client/server slice

**Intent**

On top of the independently verified Effect runtime, finish a manually started end-to-end daemon contract and client. Make untrusted ingress, replay, command correlation, disconnect semantics, and rolling wire compatibility explicit before adding process lifecycle automation.

**Implementation outline**

1. Define every wire record with Effect `Schema`: player/device/track state, hello, revision ranges, capabilities, requests, events, responses, and stable protocol errors. Decode unknown values with Effect decoders at both client and server ingress; remove manual casts/parallel validators that can drift from schemas.
2. Change hello compatibility from package-version equality to protocol major plus supported revision interval and capability intersection. Negotiate the highest overlapping revision. Package version remains diagnostic metadata. The initial revision supports itself; future additive updates retain the immediately preceding revision for rolling upgrades.
3. Return an actionable typed incompatibility containing both supported ranges. A healthy server remains authoritative after rejecting an incompatible client.
4. Preserve immediate status/latest-state replay. Carry daemon instance ID and monotonic revision on snapshots; the client rejects older revisions, wrong daemon IDs, duplicate/out-of-order responses, and all frames from a superseded connection generation.
5. Enforce maximum frame size, UTF-8/NDJSON completion, hello-first ordering, strictly increasing request IDs, capability/action checks, seek bounds, and stable success/error envelopes. Malformed clients are isolated without disturbing the listener or healthy peers.
6. Keep the global FIFO and authoritative toggle semantics from Phase 1. A successful play/pause/seek projects centrally before delayed reconciliation; next/previous reconcile promptly. Queue overflow and provider failure have typed responses and the queue continues.
7. Make the explicit client settle every pending request exactly once. A connection loss before a response yields a typed indeterminate/connection-lost result; commands are never replayed. Public Promise/callback subscriptions may remain as the host adapter, with idempotent disposal and listener-failure isolation.
8. Build the Node-targeted daemon executable and verify the package contains all runtime files while excluding tests/scripts.

