## Whole-run definition of done

- `@naxodev/music-core` ships a Node-compatible machine-local daemon and client with a schema-validated, versioned, bounded Unix-socket protocol.
- The daemon's provider, listener, socket, accepted connections, event flow, command lane, poll/retry schedules, and shutdown are owned by Context services, Layers, scopes, supervised fibers/streams, and Effect state primitives—not imperative objects wrapped in `Effect.scoped`.
- Runtime settings cross an Effect `Config` boundary, expected internal failures are `Schema.TaggedErrorClass` values, interruption is preserved, and TestClock deterministically proves every timing policy.
- The isolated packed-install smoke starts the real executable with `node`, completes hello/replay, and observes clean idle shutdown/socket cleanup.
- Concurrent first use creates one safe same-user daemon. Stale artifacts, signals, defects, and zero-client shutdown release all resources exactly once.
- Supported old/current clients negotiate and share the live daemon. An unsupported client fails actionably without unlinking, killing, replacing, or retry-looping against it.
- A tested 24-client scenario proves one provider/stream/poll owner, immediate replay, bounded slow-client isolation, and one cross-client FIFO.
- Reconnect accepts a replacement daemon's replay, rejects old-generation data, settles pending commands truthfully, and never silently replays an indeterminate command.
- OpenCode and Pi no longer create providers or own provider restart, fallback polling, provider playback clocks, stale-sample lanes, or general transport queues. Each disposes only its client and presentation resources.
- Existing complete-snapshot behavior, coalesced recovery, 3/5/8 polling, 1/2/4/8 stream restart, stale-result rejection, fallback provider behavior, controls, errors, waveform, artwork identity/cache/rendering, reload, and shutdown semantics remain green at their new owner.
